Usage: remuda cluster <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init       Create this node identity and listen on a private LAN address by default (port 7441). Example: remuda cluster init --no-listen
  invite     Create an invitation for another node. Example: remuda cluster invite
  join       Join using a quoted invitation line; a fingerprint is needed when stdin is not a terminal. Example: remuda cluster join 'remuda-join-v1 …'
  nodes      List the nodes known to this cluster. Example: remuda cluster nodes
  alias      Set or clear a local display alias for a node. Example: remuda cluster alias node-abcd1234 macbook
  control    Enable or disable remote control. Example: remuda cluster control off
  revoke     Revoke a node or fingerprint; prompt before revoking unless --yes is used. Example: remuda cluster revoke <NODE>
  remote     Attach to a remote session, or show the remote session picker. Example: remuda cluster remote node/session
  listen     Manage the cluster listener. Example: remuda cluster listen --bind 127.0.0.1
  call       Call a remote node API. Example: remuda cluster call <NODE> list --addr 192.0.2.1
  help       Print help for a cluster command

